  "text": "Beneath the lamps’ ethereal, pale light,\nHe walked the streets where shadows bite.\nEach footfall echoed, stark and clear,\nOn pavement cold and empty here.\n\nLike ghosts, the crowds drifted by,\nWith vacant eyes and passing sigh.\nTheir faces buried, deep and wide,\nIn worlds of their own, far from his side.\n\nAmidst the urban, rushing sea,\nHe stood alone, a solitary tree.\nA profound solitude, deep and vast,\nWatching the city moments pass.\n\nThe animal known for its long neck is the giraffe."
